This project includes a transfer-planning formulation adapted from
open-fpl-solver by Solio Analytics (https://github.com/solioanalytics/open-fpl-solver),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSES/open-fpl-solver-Apache-2.0.txt).
Changes: rewritten for a single manager around our own projections; lean variable set
(single bench indicator, vice-captain and bench order set after solving from next
gameweek's projections only); diminishing value of banked free transfers; a safety
margin on hits; chip opportunity costs ("hold values") instead of chip limits only.

Historical data for backtests comes from vaastav/Fantasy-Premier-League
(https://github.com/vaastav/Fantasy-Premier-League) and is downloaded at run time,
not redistributed. Live data comes from the public Fantasy Premier League API.
